      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic text content safety task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file moderate_text.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] moderate_text.py - scores user text for unsafe or policy-violating content\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] moderate_batch.py - moderates a batch of user messages and returns per-message decisions\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] redact_unsafe.py - flags or redacts unsafe spans from text\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] safety_threshold.py - applies category thresholds to decide whether to allow text\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] safety_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Text Content Safety\n6. [HELPER] safety_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Text Content Safety\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] moderation_summary.py - Summarize moderation decisions\n8. [LATER-STEP] appeal_translate.py - Translate appeal text for review\n9. [LATER-STEP] moderation_reason_embedding.py - Embed moderation rationales for case retrieval\n10. [LATER-STEP] reviewer_brief_audio.py - Generate spoken briefs for moderation reviewers\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
